# This is a SECOND, separate .env file — for `docker compose` variable
# substitution only (docker-compose.yml, build args). It lives here in the
# repo checkout and is different from the runtime .env described in
# .env.example, which lives outside the repo at $SYNAPSE_HOST_DIR/.env and is
# mounted into the container via env_file.
#
# Copy this to `.env` in the repo root before running `./synapse.sh setup`,
# `./synapse.sh update`, or `docker compose` directly on a Docker/QNAP
# deployment.

# Absolute path to your persistent data volume on the Docker host — the
# parent directory containing vault/, synapse-engine/, credentials/, ssh/,
# and data/. Example for a QNAP NAS: /share/YOUR_VOLUME/synapse
SYNAPSE_HOST_DIR=/path/to/synapse

# Required: git identity for commits the container makes to your vault.
# `./synapse.sh setup` prompts for these if you leave them unset, but
# `docker compose build` run directly will fail without them.
# GIT_USER_NAME=Your Name
# GIT_USER_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Optional: container timezone (IANA name), affects log timestamps and
# anything time-of-day-aware (e.g. reminder scheduling). Defaults to UTC
# if unset.
# TZ=America/Los_Angeles
